@dami1A Confirmed with complete HTTP Request 4.2 workflows on **2.41.7 and 2.46.6**, using loopback UTF-8 JSON fixtures: both modes finish successfully and every HTTP response is 200. Auto corrupts your French example and `Küçük`; changing only Response Format to JSON preserves all six records.

[Runnable workflow exports, the same case, and JSON/JUnit results](https://github.com/blucca/n8n-check/tree/6dc3fd1/examples/http-utf8). ASCII, Czech, separated-guillemet and literal-U+FFFD controls remain intact in these runs. The README also has a manual two-version Action for reruns.

Is the historical row cleanup your next task?
